  "body": "What happens: on Windows, `no_skims_is_the_rough_program_and_json_unchanged` in `crates/app/tests/wire_post.rs` can fail. Host `winnie`, main `f0bdc5109`:\n\n```\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\wire_post.rs:330:63:\nthe wire program posts: \"cannot write C:\\Users\\...\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\camcraft-wire-skims-7908.nc: Access is denied. (os error 5)\"\n```\n\nCause: `post_text()` (line 329) writes to `camcraft-wire-skims-<process id>.nc`. Several tests call it, and they run in parallel threads of one process, so they use the same path. Windows refuses a write while another thread holds or deletes the file. macOS and Linux permit it, so the test passes there.\n\nFix: give each call its own file (a `tempfile` directory). The other temp names in this file are used by one test each.\n\nDone means: `post_text()` uses a unique path for each call, and `wire_post` passes on Windows.\n",
